WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.060
My first thought when I saw the new 2019 iPad
Air show up on Apple’s website was, wow,

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:11.089
this thing’s basically a 2017 iPad Pro but
with fewer features, so I recommended that

00:00:11.089 --> 00:00:15.870
instead of the new Air, but since then, I’ve
realized that not everyone wants a used or

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:21.550
refurbished 2-year old iPad, and although
the A10X chip in the iPad Pro will last many

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:26.330
years, the A12 in the new iPad Air will last
longer, and it’s fresh and brand new.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:31.100
I’ve realized that the $500 price tag really
isn’t that bad for what you get, considering

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.870
that the extra power of the 2018 iPad Pro
won’t be noticed unless you’re doing something

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:37.250
like video editing.

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:41.129
We played games on both iPads and didn’t
really notice a difference in available graphics

00:00:41.129 --> 00:00:43.980
quality and smoothness of gameplay.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:49.539
Both of them could easily play certain games
at 60 frames per second and even PUBG at maxed

00:00:49.539 --> 00:00:50.760
out graphics.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:52.879
No issues at all on the iPad Air.

00:00:52.879 --> 00:00:59.160
The 2019 iPad Mini packs the same A12 processor
as the iPad Air but for $100 cheaper, which

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.289
is a great deal if you’re okay with the
smaller display, and in my review of the iPad

00:01:03.289 --> 00:01:08.930
Mini, I called it the best tablet ever for
gaming, even more so than the new iPad Pro,

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:11.810
because of the lightweight and easy to hold
form factor.

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:17.040
The Mini and Air are basically identical iPads
except for two things, the size and the fact

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.600
that the Air gets a smart connector for use
with Apple’s high-quality smart keyboard.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:25.720
The Mini is so small that typing on a Bluetooth
keyboard won’t really be comfortable at

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:26.720
all.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:28.790
Other than that, they’re the same exact
iPad.

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:34.570
The displays are absolutely fantastic and
much better than the 2018 budget iPads display.

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:39.040
However, the smaller display of the Mini is
definitely a drawback for certain things,

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:43.260
so that’s why it’s worth it for some people
to pay the extra $100 for iPad Air.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:47.260
If you’re into note taking or drawing, the
Mini’s display feels pretty limiting in

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:48.260
that regard.

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:52.290
I don’t think people realize just how much
smaller the display is compared to the iPad

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:53.290
Air.

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:57.740
Video content is much smaller, doing schoolwork
or spreadsheets may be a bit more difficult

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:00.009
and you see less on the screen while browsing
the web.

00:02:00.009 --> 00:02:05.030
So the 2019 iPad Air is a great choice for
those who need a larger display but don’t

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:07.090
want to pay for the new iPad Pro.

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:11.190
The biggest problem is that iOS is currently
very limiting so you can’t really use your

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:14.580
iPad as a computer replacement, at least not
yet.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:18.411
Now let’s take a look at what we can expect
in the future.

00:02:18.411 --> 00:02:22.320
iOS 13 is gonna be revealed soon, and it looks
like there are some iPad features coming that

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:25.070
are gonna boost productivity and multitasking
on the iPad.

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:29.350
Of course, there’s the rumored Dark Mode
feature, but I want to focus on productivity

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:30.350
features.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:34.170
For example, it looks like we’re finally
getting multiple app window support.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:41.570
So that means you can have two instances of
google docs open, or two safari windows, two

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:45.780
spreadsheets, and much more, and you can move
them around the screen, just like you can

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.120
do on a real computer.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:53.400
Safari will be able to automatically ask for
a desktop version of websites to avoid compatibility

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.400
issues on certain websites.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:58.450
And we’re finally getting a real undo gesture,
because who’s gonna be shaking their iPad

00:02:58.450 --> 00:02:59.570
to undo text.

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:00.690
That’s ridiculous.

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:05.030
Apple’s also rumored to be adding a new
font manager, and they’re making improvements

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:08.040
to document collaboration in third-party apps.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:12.600
The Mail app is getting some worthy desktop-like
improvements as well, and it seems like Apple

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:17.500
is finally gonna add a way to quickly select
multiple items in various views, just like

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:18.500
click and drag works on macOS.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:19.500
We should also expect a new and much more
useful volume HUD as well since the current

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:20.500
one really sucks.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.660
As you can tell from these changes, Apple
is really focusing on improving workflow and

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:27.240
allowing people to actually replace their
laptops much more easily.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:31.690
Now if you’re using these features and working
with multiple windows, being limited to the

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:33.510
iPad Mini’s display isn’t gonna be fun.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:38.020
That’s why I think the Air is the better
choice for people who do use it for studying,

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:40.660
typing, business or multitasking.

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:44.510
And we can even look further to iOS 14 and
what features that’ll be adding.

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:48.250
I’m sure the extra screen real estate will
serve you better in the years to come.

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:52.150
Now if you don’t do much of that, like let’s
say you do a lot of gaming, and you like the

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:56.790
portability of the iPad Mini, then that’s
still a great choice for some people, especially

00:03:56.790 --> 00:03:58.040
since you save $100.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:03.400
And talking about the new iPad Pro, I still
think it’s overkill for almost everyone,

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:06.040
even after iOS 13 and 14 are released.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:10.250
The A12 in the iPad Air is a very powerful
chip and it’ll be more than good enough

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.950
for most people for years to come.

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:15.470
Now what are some drawbacks of the 2019 iPad
Air?

00:04:15.470 --> 00:04:20.070
Well, the main thing is that it’s still
using the same old home button-packing design.

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:22.320
To me, it’s really not that big of a deal.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.060
The design still looks, feels and works great.

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:29.690
Another downside is that it’s only packing
two speakers on the bottom, unlike 4 speakers

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:30.930
on the iPad Pro.

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:35.210
It sucks but it makes sense why Apple would
keep that exclusively for the iPad Pro, just

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:36.900
like the ProMotion technology.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:39.730
Other than that, there’s really nothing
to complain about with the iPad Air.

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:44.430
It’s a fantastic all-around iPad that offers
basically everything you’ll need to do iPad

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:47.530
things, with an incredibly bright and color
accurate display.

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:48.610
So here’s my recommendation.

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:54.310
If you don’t care much for the iPad Pro’s
extra features and you want to do some drawing,

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:58.820
note-taking, typing or multitasking, I would
definitely buy the new iPad Air over every

00:04:58.820 --> 00:05:01.850
other iPad in Apple’s 2019 lineup.

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:09.220
Now if your budget is limited, you can pick
up the 2018 budget iPad for only around $250-$280

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:13.650
brand new, but you’ll have to compromise
on things like display quality and a bit of

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:14.650
performance.

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:17.290
If you enjoyed this review, make sure to hit
that button to subscribe and check out some

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:19.490
of our in-depth iPad comparison videos.

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:25.120
Thanks for watching, and we’ll see you in
the next video.

